Re-check requests without the ledger. Today `pull()` (bin/lib/fm_autopilot.py:364-374, the trigger at :371-373) calls `recheck()` only on the poll that sees a head change, and `once()` makes that the only attempt. After this task a head change records which reviewers still need asking, and every poll at that head works the list until it is empty:
- New state field `data['rechecked']` (default `{}`, added to the defaults dict in `Pilot.__init__`, bin/lib/fm_autopilot.py:63-65) maps the PR number (string) to `{head, names}`.
- In `pull()`, when `old['head'] != head` (the existing trigger), it sets `data['rechecked'][number] = dict(head=head, names=[...])` with every policy reviewer (`policy['reviewers']`) who has a prior review on another commit and none at the head, the same selection `recheck()` makes at :337-339. Then, on every poll where `data['rechecked'][number]['head'] == head`, `pull()` calls `recheck(task, pr, reviews)`, which works only on the recorded names.
- `policy['post'] == 'local'` keeps today's behaviour exactly: it queues 'Reviewer re-check needed: <name>' with identity `key(['recheck', pr['number'], pr['head']['sha'], name])`, exactly today's value (built at bin/lib/fm_autopilot.py:340, queued at :342) (the integer PR number from the payload, not `pull()`'s string `number`, because `key()` hashes them differently) and removes the name (queue() already skips a known identity).
- Otherwise, per name: if the name (case-insensitive) is in this poll's `pr['requested_reviewers']` logins (the `pulls/<n>` payload `pull()` receives; GitHub returns `requested_reviewers` as a list of user objects with `login`), or the reviewer now has a review whose `commit_id` is the head, it is done: remove it, no request. If the retry token `recheck-<name lowercased>:<number>:<head>` is not due, skip it. Otherwise POST through `self.probe(self.gh('api', '-X', 'POST', 'repos/<repository>/pulls/<number>/requested_reviewers', '-f', 'reviewers[]=<name>', '--include'))` and read the HTTP status line from stdout the way `update_branch` does (bin/lib/fm_autopilot_branches.py:139-146).
  - 201: remove the name and delete its retry token.
  - 422: GitHub refused the request (the user is not a collaborator, or is the PR author); retrying cannot help. Remove the name and queue one wake now, identity `recheck-refused-<number>-<head>-<name>`, text '<task> #<number> reviewer re-check refused: <name>: <message>' with the `message` field of the JSON body, bilingual like the other wakes.
  - Anything else (another status, no status line, or an `ERRORS` exception): `branch_failure('recheck-' + name.lower(), number, head, task, line)`, so attempts come at offsets 0, 1 and 3, then one wake. Login names cannot contain ':', so the token splits correctly in `prune_branches`.
- A head change replaces the record (the old head's names no longer apply), and `prune_branches` drops it on a head change or a terminal PR: add 'rechecked' to the tuple at bin/lib/fm_autopilot_branches.py:19. A record whose `names` is empty may stay until pruned.
