Stubs answer like GitHub and gh (repo rule: a stub written from the code hides the bug it should catch). `gh api ... --include` prints the status line and headers, a blank line and the body on stdout. On HTTP 4xx/5xx it also exits 1 and prints `gh: <message> (HTTP <code>)` on stderr. Use these exact bodies:
- 201 for POST requested_reviewers: status line `HTTP/2.0 201 Created`, body the pull request JSON with `requested_reviewers: [{"login": "alice", ...}]`;
- 422 not a collaborator: body `{"message":"Reviews may only be requested from collaborators. One or more of the users or teams you specified is not a collaborator of the owner/repo repository.","documentation_url":"https://docs.github.com/rest/pulls/review-requests#request-reviewers-for-a-pull-request","status":"422"}`;
- 422 author: body `{"message":"Review cannot be requested from pull request author.","documentation_url":"https://docs.github.com/rest/pulls/review-requests#request-reviewers-for-a-pull-request","status":"422"}`;
- 503: status line `HTTP/2.0 503 Service Unavailable`.
